            ]
          },
          "worked": "The domain is $x>0$. Change to base 2.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_2(x)+\\frac{\\log_2(x)}{\\log_2(4)}&=6\\\\\\log_2(x)+\\frac12\\log_2(x)&=6\\\\\\frac32\\log_2(x)&=6\\\\\\log_2(x)&=4\\\\x&=2^4\\\\x&=16\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $16>0$, the solution is valid.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 70
      },
